  "title": "Derivatives Strategy: (Delta-)hedging your hedges",
  "type": "derivatives",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-08-18",
  "insights": [
   "Delta-hedging long put positions can improve the efficiency of option-based hedges by monetizing volatility spikes and reducing the carry burden of traditional protective puts.",
   "The strategy is most effective against sharp equity drawdowns accompanied by volatility spikes, but performs poorly in slow, grind-lower equity environments where volatility remains subdued.",
   "Skew-adjusted delta hedging, which accounts for the downward-sloping volatility skew, can further reduce negative carry compared to standard Black-Scholes delta hedging, improving overall convexity.",
   "Delta-hedging transforms directional option exposure into a position driven by higher-order Greeks like gamma and vega, making it a dynamic process requiring periodic rebalancing.",
   "UBS maintains a constructive view on equities, supported by strong earnings growth and AI-related investment, despite risks from potential loss of confidence in AI, weaker economic performance, and elevated financing costs."
  ],
